message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: article
title: "Agent Mesh: Governed Decentralized Coordination Under Partial Information"
authors:
  - family-names: Rodriguez
    given-names: Douglas
    email: douglas.rodriguez@trafilea.com
date-released: 2026-08-17
version: 1.1.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Agentplat/agentplat"
keywords:
  - multi-agent systems
  - decentralized coordination
  - agent governance
  - controlled emergence
  - distributed systems
abstract: >-
  Agent Mesh is a provider-neutral coordination substrate for independently
  executing agents operating with bounded local state and partial information.
  The paper specifies a reference composition that separates evidence,
  planning, agreement, assignment authority, and authorization of protected
  external effects. Version 1.1 adds the receipt-producing governed runtime,
  partition and topology policy, approval checkpoints, continuity and
  compromise response, while retaining an inconclusive preregistered
  evaluation as a study-instrument postmortem rather than a comparative claim.
